{"name":"Etcetera","hex":"#e1c6d4","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"etcetera","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Phrase","definitions":["Alternative form of et cetera."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Alternative form of et cetera."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/etcetera"}],"entries":[{"title":"Etcetera (TV program)","blocks":[{"text":"Etcetera is a Philippine lifestyle and magazine show produced by Solar Entertainment Corporation and broadcast by ETC from October 23, 2011, to December 3, 2015."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/1/19/Etcetera2014titlecard.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Etcetera_(TV_program)"},{"title":"Etcetera (song)","blocks":[{"text":"\"Etcetera\" is an unreleased song recorded as a demo by Paul McCartney on 20 August 1968, during a session for The Beatles."}],"link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Etcetera_(song)"},{"title":"Et cetera","blocks":[{"text":"Et cetera, abbreviated to etc. or et cet., is a Latin expression that is used in English to mean \"and all the rest\". The ampersand \"&\" is a ligature of \"et\", thus it can also be abbreviated &c. . Translated literally from Latin, et can mean 'and', while cētĕra can mean 'the rest'; thus, the expression translates to 'and the rest'."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/5/55/Cromwellcoin.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Et_cetera"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/thumb/7/75/Etceteraetc.jpg/120px-Etceteraetc.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/7/75/Etceteraetc.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/thumb/7/75/Etceteraetc.jpg/120px-Etceteraetc.j